course: dictionary
lesson: 8067
title: Relay
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A relay is a race between teams. Each runner or swimmer does one part, then passes on to the next, often by handing over a baton. «Each runner ran one lap, then passed the baton on.» The words race, runner and baton tell you it is a sports word.
explain: Relay can also be a verb, which means to pass something on to someone else. «Please relay this message to your parents.» The word message tells you that relay means to pass the message on, not to race.
explain: The word can also be a noun for a device that passes on signals, or a switch in an electric circuit. Science words like circuit or signal are your clue. In the phrase «in relays», it means in turns, with groups taking over from each other.
fact: A relay race is a race between teams, where each person runs or swims one part.
fact: A baton is the stick or object that is handed on in a relay race.
fact: To relay a message means to pass it on to someone else.
fact: «Relays» in the phrase «in relays» means in turns, one group taking over from the next.
fact: About 2,500 years ago, the Persian Royal Road had rest stations where fresh riders carried messages in relays.
fact: The Mongols had relay stations with fresh horses, so messengers could ride hundreds of kilometres a day.
fact: The Parkes radio telescope in New South Wales helped relay television pictures of the Apollo 11 Moonwalk to the world in 1969.
exercise: In the sports day race, each runner does one lap and then hands the baton to the next. What kind of race is this? | A swimming race with no teams | A long-distance race run by one person | A game of tag | *A relay race
exercise: «Please relay this message to your parents.» What does relay mean here? | *Pass the message on to them | Write the message in bright colours | Shout the message across the playground | Forget the message
exercise: «The Persian Royal Road had rest stations where fresh riders carried messages in relays.» What does «in relays» mean? | In a straight line, all at the same time | Very slowly and quietly | In secret, so nobody knows | *In turns, with each group taking over from the last
test: «The Mongols had relay stations with fresh horses so that messengers could ride hundreds of kilometres a day.» Why were there relay stations? | So the roads could be made wider | So the messengers could stop riding for good | *So messengers could change to fresh horses and keep going | So the horses could sleep all day
test: Relay also has a meaning in science. Which of these is a relay? | A tall tower that stores water | A kind of cheese | A soft cloth for cleaning glass | *A switch that passes on a signal in an electric circuit
exam: Which sentence uses relay as a verb, meaning to pass something on? | *Please relay the news to Grandma | The relay race starts at noon | The relay runners wore green shirts | The relay switch clicked on
